  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Dative and accusative together",
     "texto": [
      "With verbs like **schenken** (to give as a present), **geben** (to give) and **zeigen** (to show), the **dative** (to whom) comes first and then the **accusative** (what): **Ich schenke meiner Mutter Blumen** (I'm giving my mother flowers). Question words: **Wem?** (to whom?) and **Was?** (what?).",
      "With pronouns the order changes: the accusative goes before the dative: **Ich gebe es ihm** (I'm giving it to him)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Pronouns in the dative",
     "texto": [
      "You've already seen: **mir**, **dir**, **ihm**, **ihr**, **uns**, **euch**, **Ihnen**, **ihnen**. With **ihr** (to her) the verb can come after: **Ich schenke ihr Blumen**.",
      "Watch out for the false friend: **geben** means \"to give\", not \"to be\"."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
